\label{sec:split-groth-groups}



For a small additive category $\modC $, the {\em split Grothendieck group}
$K_0(\modC )$ of $\modC $ is the abelian group generated by the
isomorphism classes of objects of $\modC $ with relations $[x\oplus
y]_{\cong}=[x]_{\cong}+[y]_{\cong}$ for $x,y\in \Ob(\modC)$.  Here
$[x]_{\cong}$ denotes the isomorphism class of $x$.  The split
Grothendieck group $K_0$ defines a functor from additive categories to abelian groups. Here the morphisms in the category of additive categories are additive  functors.

